---
// The one-line CTA repeated at the foot of Home and every long-form page
// (DESIGN_BRIEF.md 5.1 section 6, and re-used elsewhere as the established
// foot of the site — see BUILD-PLAN.md step 5). Previously this exact three
// line block was hand-copied into eleven separate .astro files; changing the
// line or the button text meant editing all eleven. One component now.
//
// Copy changed 2026-07-31 (Kristen Hitch review, DESIGN_BRIEF 5.8/5.9):
//   - The line was "Ready to start your project?" — a question the reader can
//     answer "no" to. Now "Let's Get Started," which is an invitation.
//   - The button was "Schedule a Consultation," which asked for the paid
//     in-home visit as the first step. Booking is now a two-step funnel and
//     the site's job is step one: the free discovery call. This exact wording
//     is the primary site-wide CTA and it should match everywhere.
//
// TODO (backend, pending — do not implement without a decision):
//   1. The href points at /contact until the calendar booking tool for the
//      discovery call is chosen. Calendly vs Google Calendar is an open
//      question with Amy (ASK-AMY.md). When it is answered, this becomes the
//      booking link and the qualification form stays as the fallback.
//   2. The automated confirmation email after a booking is a separate,
//      coupled decision. Not built. The consultation fee figure belongs in
//      that email and NOWHERE on this site (5.9).
//
// Optional props (2026-10-08, COPY-PASS-V1 Tasks 7 and 8): a page can swap in
// its own closing heading and paragraph (Process, Contact) and point the same
// button somewhere else (Contact's in-page anchor to the form). With no props
// it is exactly the band it always was. The copy itself comes from each
// page's content file; nothing page-specific is written here.

interface Props {
  heading?: string;
  body?: string[];
  href?: string;
}

const { heading, body = [], href = '/contact' } = Astro.props;
---

<section class="section wrap contact-band bg-ground">
  {heading ? (
    <div class="contact-band__copy">
      <h2 class="type-display contact-band__line contact-band__heading">{heading}</h2>
      {body.map((paragraph) => <p class="contact-band__body">{paragraph}</p>)}
    </div>
  ) : (
    <p class="type-display contact-band__line">Let's Get Started</p>
  )}
  <a href={href} class="btn btn-solid">Schedule your complimentary discovery call</a>
</section>
